response:
 The desired point  $P$ divides the line segment  $\overline{AB}$ into two parts  $\overline{AP}$ and  $\overline{PB}$ so that  $AP:PB = 3:2.$ Then the following diagram arises:

[asy]
unitsize(1 cm);

pair A, B, P;

A = (0,0);
B = (5,1);
P = (3/5)*A+(2/5)*B;

draw(A--B);

dot("$A$", A, S);
dot("$B$", B, S);
dot("$P$", P, S);
draw((3/5)*A+(2/5)*B--A);

label<pair("We are given $AP:PB=3:2, \ \textrm{so} \ AP=\frac{3}{5}AB,$

draw arrow=(ThickArrow Bedford)$ and similarly $PB=\frac{2}{5}AB$*);

[/asy]Since $\begin{aligned}
\overrightarrow{AP}&=&\frac{3}{5}\overrightarrow{AB},\\
\overrightarrow{AB}&=&\overrightarrow{PB}-\overrightarrow{PA},
\end{aligned}$it follows that $\overrightarrow{AP}=\frac{3}{5}\overrightarrow{PB}$ and $\overrightarrow{PA}=-\frac{3}{5}\overrightarrow{PB}$. So   $$\begin{aligned}\overrightarrow{PB}&=&\overrightarrow{PA}+\overrightarrow{AB} \\ &=&-\frac{3}{5}\overrightarrow{PB}+\frac{2}{5}\overrightarrow{PB}+\frac{3}{5}\overrightarrow{AB}\\&=&-\frac{3}{5}\overrightarrow{PB}+\frac{2}{5}\overrightarrow{PB} + \frac{3}{5}\overrightarrow{AP}+\frac{3}{5}\overrightarrow{PB}\\&=&-\frac{1}{5}\overrightarrow{PB} + \frac{3}{5}\overrightarrow{PB} + \frac{3}{5}\overrightarrow{AP}\end{aligned}$$or   $$\overrightarrow{PB}=\frac{5}{4}\overrightarrow{AP}$$on which is divided by applying the distributive law, yielding   $$\overrightarrow{PA}=\frac{1}{4}\overrightarrow{PB}.$$
Finally, from the definition of the weighted average $P = tA+uB,$ using the calculations above    $$\overrightarrow{P}=\frac{3}{5}\overrightarrow{B} + \frac{2}{5}\overrightarrow{A},$$so $\boxed{\left(\tfrac{2}{5},\tfrac{3}{5}\right)}$ are the desired numbers. [/asy]

